Patch @vanillagreen/pi-tool-renderer so the tool_batch tool runs its calls
through the session's tool registry instead of the built-in tool constructors.

The upstream batch builds read/grep/find/ls/bash from the pi agent module, so a
batched grep or find bypasses the registered tool: with FFF in override mode a
direct grep is FFF's, while the same grep inside a batch is pi's built-in. A
batch that routes through ctx.executeTool runs one implementation, and the
nested calls get the same argument validation, tool_call/tool_result hooks, and
permission checks as model-issued calls. A context without executeTool keeps the
built-in path.

Applied by flake/packages.nix after npm install. To apply it to a development
checkout, run from the repository root:

  patch -p1 -d node_modules/@vanillagreen/pi-tool-renderer < patches/pi-tool-renderer-batch-registry.patch

Upstream: github.com/vanillagreencom/kendex

